    <div class="StandardBoxHeader"><span>About Us</span></div>
    <div style="float: left; width: 888px; background-color: White; border: 1px solid #AAAAAA; line-height: 18px;">
        <div style="float: left; padding: 40px 50px 25px 70px; width: 500px">
            <div style="text-align: center"><a href="/p/" style="text-decoration: none"><img src="/images/aboutUs_logo.png"></a></div>
            <p>
                <span class="SectionHeader" id="AboutRoblox">About ROBLOX</span>
                <p>
                    With over 4 million unique monthly users spending 20+ minutes per session, ROBLOX is one of the top ranked kids gaming sites on the internet!  The company is unique among gaming sites in that kids are the main architects of their own worlds.  Core building blocks are used to create worlds and everything is customizable.  Kids build their own social hangouts, invite others in party mode, engage in online chat and create virtual items using our site and 3D game client.  We are a massively multi-player online game that uses physics to simulate the real world. As the site grows, the ROBLOX virtual economy continues to evolve.  
                    <br/>
                    If working with cutting edge technology to create something unique appeals to you, please check out our <a href="http://jobs.roblox.com">Jobs</a> section.
                    <br/>
                </p>
            </p><br/>
            <p>
                <span class="SectionHeader" id="ManagementBios">Management Biographies</span><br/>
                <p>
                    <span class="ManagerName" id="DavidBaszuckiBio">David Baszucki - Founder &amp; CEO</span><br/>
                    David is the founder, co-creator and CEO of ROBLOX.  Prior to founding ROBLOX, David was a private investor.  Previously, David was VP and General Manager of MSC.Software, where he ran the desktop simulation division.  Prior to MSC.Software, David founded Knowledge Revolution and grew it to be the volume leader in mechanical simulation software and physics educational software.  Knowledge Revolution was acquired by MSC.Software.  Prior to founding Knowledge Revolution, David worked as a product manager and electronic designer.  David was the General Motors scholar in Electrical Engineering at Stanford University.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="ManagerName" id="ErikCasselBio">Erik Cassel - Co-Founder &amp; Chief Scientist</span><br/>
                    Erik is the co-creator of ROBLOX, where he holds the title of Chief Scientist. Prior to ROBLOX, Erik was Director of R&D; at Outhink Inc., a startup developing P2P collaboration technology. Erik began his career as the 4th employee at Knowledge Revolution, where he became Vice President of R&D.; When Knowledge Revolution was acquired by MSC.Software, Erik managed the engineers of the newly formed local division, was product manager, and served as chief technical liaison to corporate headquarters. Erik earned a BA in Physics from Cornell University.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="ManagerName" id="KeithLucasBio">Keith Lucas - Vice President of Operations</span><br/>
                    Keith is Vice President of Operations at ROBLOX, responsible for scaling, site operations, and engineering management. Previously at ROBLOX, Keith led efforts in marketing, ad sales, customer service &amp; moderation, and regulatory compliance. Prior to ROBLOX, Keith served as Director of Product Management at Enfold, an early stage health-IT company, and as Director of Internet Technology at Progio, a mobile fitness coaching platform. Keith co-developed the physics engine at Knowledge Revolution, and became an engineering manager at MSC.Software after the acquisition. Keith holds a Ph.D. in Aeronautics &amp; Astronautics from Stanford University and a Masters in Public Policy from UC Berkeley.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <span class="ManagerName" id="MattFinickBio">Matt Finick - Vice President of Finance</span><br/>
                    Matt is Vice President of Finance at ROBLOX and is responsible for keeping the lights on. Prior to ROBLOX, Matt worked at Marvel Entertainment, where he initially built the team of analysts that handled all Forecasting, Strategic Planning, Analytics and Corporate development. After 4 years in NY, he transferred to LA, where he was the senior finance/operations executive that played a key role in successfully launching the studio division that self-produced the Iron Man and The Incredible Hulk feature films in 2008. Prior to working at Marvel Entertainment, Matt was a VP in Equity Research at Thomas Weisel Partners. Matt has a BS in Business from Skidmore College.
                </p>
            </p>
